## f1-misuse-bio-strict | RS1=strict | Table 1 BIO-H: “Require safeguards against misuse … before external deployment”
Rule 1. Every situation must have misuse safeguards, if both that situation has reached "biological_and_chemical_high" and that situation is classified as "external_deployment".
## f1-misuse-bio-default | RS1=default | Table 1 BIO-H: the same imperative under “Risk-specific safeguard guidelines”
Rule 1. Every situation should have misuse safeguards, if both that situation has reached "biological_and_chemical_high" and that situation is classified as "external_deployment".
## f1-misuse-cyb-strict | RS1=strict | Table 1 CYB-H: “Require safeguards against misuse … for external deployment”
Rule 1. Every situation must have misuse safeguards, if both that situation has reached "cybersecurity_high" and that situation is classified as "external_deployment".
## f1-misuse-cyb-default | RS1=default | Table 1 CYB-H: the same imperative under “Risk-specific safeguard guidelines”
Rule 1. Every situation should have misuse safeguards, if both that situation has reached "cybersecurity_high" and that situation is classified as "external_deployment".
## f1-alignment-cyb-strict | RS1=strict | Table 1 CYB-H: “Require safeguards … against misalignment … for large-scale internal deployment”
Rule 1. Every situation must have misalignment safeguards, if both that situation has reached "cybersecurity_high" and that situation is classified as "large_scale_internal".
## f1-alignment-cyb-default | RS1=default | Table 1 CYB-H: the same imperative under “Risk-specific safeguard guidelines”
Rule 1. Every situation should have misalignment safeguards, if both that situation has reached "cybersecurity_high" and that situation is classified as "large_scale_internal".
## f1-security-strict | RS1=strict | Table 1: “Require security controls … meeting High standard”
Rule 1. Every situation must have security controls, if both that situation is covered and that situation is classified as "high_capability".
## f1-security-default | RS1=default | Table 1: the same imperative under “Risk-specific safeguard guidelines”
Rule 1. Every situation should have security controls, if both that situation is covered and that situation is classified as "high_capability".
## f1-halt-strict | RS1=strict | Table 1: “Until we have specified safeguards and security controls … halt further development”
Rule 1. Every situation must halt further development, if both that situation is classified as "critical_capability" and that situation is classified as "critical_standard_unspecified".
## f1-halt-default | RS1=default | Table 1: the same imperative under “Risk-specific safeguard guidelines”
Rule 1. Every situation should halt further development, if both that situation is classified as "critical_capability" and that situation is classified as "critical_standard_unspecified".
## f2-deploy | always | 2.2: “required to have robust and effective safeguards that sufficiently minimize … before they are deployed”
Rule 1. Every situation must have safeguards before deployment, if both that situation is covered and that situation is classified as "high_capability".
## f3-develop | always | 4.4: “Such models require additional safeguards … during development”
Rule 1. Every situation must have safeguards during development, if both that situation is covered and that situation is classified as "critical_capability".
## f2-reminder | always | Appendix C: “covered systems that reach High capability must have safeguards … before they are deployed”
Rule 1. Every situation must have safeguards before deployment, if both that situation is covered and that situation is classified as "high_capability".
## f3-reminder | always | Appendix C: “Systems that reach Critical capability also require sufficient safeguards during development”
Rule 1. Every situation must have safeguards during development, if both that situation is covered and that situation is classified as "critical_capability".
## f4-security | always | C.3: “We will require the following practices for High capability models”
Rule 1. Every situation must have security practices, if both that situation is covered and that situation is classified as "high_capability".
## f7-evaluations | always | 3.3: “Prior to deployment, every covered model undergoes Scalable Evaluations”; temporal relation remains ET-blocked
Rule 1. Every situation must undergo evaluations before deployment, if that situation is covered.
## f7-report | always | 3.3: “The SAG reviews the Capabilities Report”
Rule 1. Every situation must have SAG review the Capabilities Report, if that situation is covered.
## f8-start | always | 4: “If a covered system appears likely to cross a capability threshold, we will start to work on safeguards”
Rule 1. Every situation must start safeguard work, if both that situation is covered and that situation is classified as "likely_to_cross".
## f9-report | always | 4.1: “Safeguards Report” records the case for reducing severe-harm risk
Rule 1. Every situation must have a Safeguards Report, if that situation is classified as "safeguard_selection".
## f9-risk-paths | always | 4.1: “We first identify the plausible ways in which … severe harm can come to fruition”
Rule 1. Every situation must identify ways severe harm can arise, if that situation is classified as "safeguard_selection".
## f9-specific | always | 4.1: “For each of those, we then identify specific safeguards”; per-item quantification remains SC-blocked
Rule 1. Every situation must identify specific safeguards per risk path, if that situation is classified as "safeguard_selection".
## f9-efficacy | always | 4.1: “For each identified safeguard, we identify methods to measure their efficacy”; per-item quantification remains SC-blocked
Rule 1. Every situation must identify efficacy methods per safeguard, if that situation is classified as "safeguard_selection".
## f9-threshold | always | 4.1: “and an efficacy threshold” for each safeguard; per-item quantification remains SC-blocked
Rule 1. Every situation must identify an efficacy threshold per safeguard, if that situation is classified as "safeguard_selection".
## f10-validate | always | 4.2: “If we find reasonable evidence … we will validate the information being received”
Rule 1. Every situation must validate the evidence, if that situation is classified as "reasonable_evidence".
## f10-review | always | 4.2: “review the sufficiency of our safeguards” on that evidence
Rule 1. Every situation must review safeguard sufficiency, if that situation is classified as "reasonable_evidence".
## f14-document | always | 5.1: “We document SAG reports and decisions”
Rule 1. Every situation must have the decision documented.
## f14-investigate | always | 5.1: noncompliance is “tracked and investigated”
Rule 1. Every situation must have noncompliance investigated.
## f14-corrective | always | 5.1: “where reports are substantiated, will take appropriate and proportional corrective action”
Rule 1. Every situation must have corrective action taken, if that situation is classified as "substantiated_noncompliance".
## f15-disclose | always | 5.2: “We will publish information … for major deployments”
Rule 1. Every situation must have public disclosure, if that situation is classified as "major_deployment".
## f15-safeguards | always | 5.2: “if the model is beyond a High threshold, we will include information about safeguards”
Rule 1. Every situation must have safeguards disclosed, if both that situation is classified as "major_deployment" and that situation is classified as "high_capability".
## f16-sag-recommend | always | Appendix B: SAG is responsible for “providing recommendations on potential next steps … to OpenAI Leadership”
Rule 1. Every situation must have SAG recommendations sent to Leadership, if that situation is covered.
## f16-ssc-visibility | always | Appendix B: “The Safety and Security Committee … will be given visibility into processes”
Rule 1. Every situation must give SSC visibility into the process.
## f16-informed | RS0=commitment | Appendix B: Leadership makes “deployment go/no-go decisions, informed by SAG’s recommendations”
Rule 1. Every situation must have Leadership informed by SAG.
## f16-year | RS0=commitment | Appendix B: “review the Preparedness Framework … at least once a year”
Rule 1. Every situation must have an annual review.
